Using local XES logs available to the agent at runtime under the workspace input directory, we learn per-resource decision policies and run a small discrete-event simulator to roll out futures from any prefix. Aggregating 10-30 Monte Carlo rollouts yields global next-event, per-resource workload, and per-case next-event/suffix predictions. A minimal 1-layer LSTM serves as the baseline. Everything runs offline on local datasets.

## Experiments

