\section{Conclusion}
\label{sec:conclusion}
We presented a resource-centric PPM agent design that learns per-resource decision policies and uses a lightweight discrete-event simulator to roll out concurrent futures. A compact case-centric LSTM baseline shows strong next-activity performance on three public logs, setting a high bar for incremental accuracy gains. The simulator promises complementary benefits: enforcing capacity constraints, providing global next-event distributions under concurrency, and forecasting resource workloads---capabilities absent in case-centric predictors.

Our ongoing work focuses on completing the end-to-end simulator evaluation, including global next-event accuracy, suffix similarity, remaining-time MAE, and workload MAPE under learned versus FIFO dispatch, and on stress-testing robustness to hidden priorities and unobserved attributes. We also plan to compare against object-centric and graph-based baselines \cite{rohrer2022predictiveop,smit2024hoegan} and to integrate simulation-based counterfactuals \cite{bocciarelli2024simulationbasedpp}. We hope these insights help the community design PPM agents that respect concurrency and resource constraints and are thus more actionable in operational settings \cite{ceravolo2024predictivepm,park2023optimizingra}.

