\section{Implementation details}
We provide additional details to facilitate reproduction. Data loading prioritizes a workspace-local input/ directory, then data/, and falls back to common absolute paths. We parse XES using PM4Py \cite{berti2023pm4pyap}, retaining fields case\_id, activity, lifecycle, timestamp, resource. Timestamps are coerced to UTC and sorted globally. Prefix features comprise five continuous dimensions per event: time delta, time since case start, normalized hour-of-day, normalized weekday, and a binary working-hours flag (Mon--Fri, 8--17). We z-normalize time deltas and time since start using training statistics and pad to a maximum prefix length of 10 with mask-aware batching.

The LSTM baseline uses embedding size 64, hidden size 128, one layer, dropout 0.2, and an output layer over the training vocabulary (plus PAD index excluded from metrics). We train with Adam (lr=1e-3), batch size 128, for 10 epochs, picking the checkpoint with the best validation Top-3 accuracy.

For the resource-centric agent, per-resource policies are multinomial logistic regressions trained on local samples; if a resource has fewer than a small threshold of samples, we back off to a global policy. Activity durations are log-normal with median fallback. The simulator advances to the next completion, sampling next activities upon resource release, selecting FIFO among eligible cases for the chosen activity, and continuing until a horizon or case completion. From any observed prefix, we aggregate 30 rollouts to form predictions.

